{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.182267Z","id":"6ea9647643c346b914bb8e6a0038982ac91d2d3df6afdae96e560d5c06c2b102","body":{"detail":"TRANSPORT_SCRIPT (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs:398) names /_clax/transport.js with no version, and static_file's fallback branch serves it with `public, max-age=3600` and no ETag (only mark.svg and mark-dot.svg otherwise land here; the bridge is ?v=<hash>, shell/ and bridge/ files are content-hashed, the contract's .d.ts are no-cache). The shell document itself is private, no-cache. While the app reaches the embedded core over loopback (until plan Task 15's scheme handler), the WebView's HTTP cache keeps the script across app and bundle updates: after an update that changes the transport's receivers (647958f22844 moved the nonce to the first argument of callResult/streamBlock/streamEnd), the old cached script reads callResult(nonce, id, r) as callResult(id, r), finds no call, and every API call and the event stream hang for up to an hour. Content-hashing beats no-cache here: the script is parser-blocking in <head>, and no-cache would add a revalidation round trip to every shell document load (time to usable), while a versioned URL in a no-cache document is always current.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":353},"content_hash":"c5127f4323a62c1928e32914480972fc9fa32a3f05cd2dc89e74b93295595947"},"suggested_fix":"Serve it as the bridge is served: write <script src=\"/_clax/transport.js?v=<short_hash of its sha256>\"> in with_embed_meta (bridge_version's shape over web.sha256(\"_clax/transport.js\")), answer IMMUTABLE at the matching v and REVALIDATE with an ETag otherwise (bridge_cache_control generalised), and pin both in crates/clax-server/tests/shell_boot.rs.","summary":"/_clax/transport.js is served unversioned with public, max-age=3600 and no ETag, so a WebView over loopback can run an hour-old transport against a newer relay","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:51.869576Z","id":"cd51a28954d24e3b65beb5f757518b22070d3b807ca417d223dca6b295a2cfdd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:20e1ed98c3fc","summary":"Shell documents of an embedded core load /_clax/transport.js?v=<short hash> (transport_version, boot::transport_script); static_file serves the transport through versioned_cache_control with an ETag, immutable at the matching v in a release build and no-cache at any other URL; asset_cache leaves it to the server. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all passed: shell_boot::an_embedded_core_marks_every_shell_document_and_frames_content_on_its_origin (versioned tag; no-cache, ETag and 304 for the bare and a stale URL; failed before the fix on the unversioned tag) and shell::tests::another_host_never_serves_the_files_named_by_version.","supersedes":"6ea9647643c346b914bb8e6a0038982ac91d2d3df6afdae96e560d5c06c2b102","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:26:56.718634Z","id":"a6eb1567a5f37fa6ee60488184c14089007f0931fd0af5f1d019e9794a54fb62","body":{"detail":"For GET /a/<id>/get, clax_http::hosted::gate answers a restricted page, a page that does not exist and a malformed ID with JSON (404 not_found, 401 sign_in_required) before the handler runs. refusals, layered outside the gate in crates/clax-server/src/router.rs wrap, turns any 401/403/404 of that path that is not text/html into the one 404 page with the /signin link, so the answers stay alike. The gate itself could render page paths' refusals as pages, for /a/<id> too, which today answers a signed-out browser with JSON.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":345},"content_hash":"7725c36be2db4c3c1d15f3cba2797219919902ab2b0e50467b44de3c2df19efe"},"summary":"The Get in Clax page's sign-in answer is made by a layer that rewrites the hosted gate's JSON refusals, not by the gate","tags":["revisit:the hosted gate renders HTML refusals for page paths","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:26:56.718753Z","id":"0d8a4931da73d6c7afddbb9812126303c0544e73bfaed2f3bff1a3e83bcba595","body":{"detail":"Nothing on the server maps an icon word to a glyph (the web shell does not draw artifact icons either), so the no-script page shows the initial. When an icon set exists, the tile should draw it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"1e5ea65cfce03a96b078f2e46336b3e931f7f643de39ead97376961985c1d626"},"summary":"The Get in Clax page draws the title's first letter in its tile; the artifact's icon word is only the tile's title attribute","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:42:13.941533Z","id":"57643210e1bd1b2d8da82453eef8a95e767a1ab625cf7b492b59e35c11f14a41","body":{"detail":"Without [hosted], origin() (get_page.rs:93-98) is the daemon's browser_base, an http:// origin such as http://localhost:7480. The page then links clax:get?url=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A<port>%2Fa%2F<id>, which BundleIntakeEvent.artifactOf (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart:84-92) refuses as not_a_link because the inner URL is not https, and the QR code encodes http://localhost:<port>/a/<id>/get, which a phone cannot reach. Seen with TestServer::spawn() (no hosted): GET /a/<id>/get answers 200 with href=\"clax:get?url=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A64222%2Fa%2F0gm50vb64hc9\". Download .clax works there.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":263},"content_hash":"34f22b6f53f8b8d62e13c24b4a929fbd4b50cb25e2c32565de53dd276339fcdf"},"suggested_fix":"When s.hosted is None, leave out the QR code and the Open in Clax link (Download .clax and Open the page stay), or serve the page only on a hosted Clax.","summary":"On a local daemon the Get in Clax page offers an Open in Clax link the app refuses and a QR code of a localhost URL","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:42:13.941622Z","id":"c8e50f8cafbce8e10175e99cf38e70995423bfc731dce4b72491134528153e25","body":{"detail":"page() refuses agents with 403 not_for_agents (JSON), and refusals, layered outside the gate, rewrites every non-HTML 401/403/404 of that path into the unavailable() page. docs/contract.md's route table says GET /a/{aid}/get answers the owner's agents 403 not_for_agents. Seen on TestServer::spawn_hosted_with: GET /a/<id>/get with Authorization: Bearer <daemon token> and X-Clax-Session: s1 answered 404 text/html, the sign-in page. A local daemon answers 403 as documented. No existence leak: the body and headers are the same for every refusal.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":320},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"221defcfdeb26be75f6b981a4a1150835ee3fe27f6be7ca26ee1079947951af4"},"suggested_fix":"Leave a not_for_agents refusal as it is (match the error code, or have page() answer agents before the layer can see them as a refusal), or render the gate's page-path refusals in the gate itself (record a6eb1567's alternative).","summary":"On a hosted Clax the owner's agent is answered 404 HTML at /a/<id>/get, not the 403 not_for_agents docs/contract.md lists","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:42:13.941661Z","id":"b0e3bc2168e0d0a4b03fba6591b3026a777968babb3aa6c09fde56361fe80640","body":{"detail":"In an Apple app site association component, * matches any characters including /, so {\"/\": \"/a/*/get\"} matches /a/<id>/v/3/get, the only path that reaches a page file published as get (crates/clax-server/src/shell/route.rs:10-15, web/shell/src/route.ts). A tap on such a link from another site opens Clax, and BundleIntakeEvent.artifactOf (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/bundle_intake.dart:73-77) refuses it as not_a_link, instead of showing the page. The Android filter's pathPattern /a/.*/get (apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:113) matches the same paths.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":362},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"52102aebb08a4ee47074c2992e2ce3af55a177cc460cf8622327567ddcf92cda"},"suggested_fix":"Match one 12-character segment: {\"/\": \"/a/????????????/get\"} (twelve ?), and the same in the Android pathPattern (/a/............/get).","summary":"The app site association's /a/*/get also claims /a/<id>/v/<n>/get, a page file named get, which the app then refuses","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:42:18.530468Z","id":"f89390fa963cd5a4d661e1c51c923ffbb0b2337f7d63473e60fb00d5f671e34c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bdfa2182d","summary":"A daemon that is not hosted now offers Download .clax alone: app_page leaves out the QR code and the clax:get link when AppState::hosted is None. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__3: get_page::get_page_on_a_local_daemon_offers_download_alone ... ok (TestServer::spawn(): no <svg, no clax:get, Download .clax is the primary button).","supersedes":"57643210e1bd1b2d8da82453eef8a95e767a1ab625cf7b492b59e35c11f14a41","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:42:18.678081Z","id":"0659649b0baa9298ce9dea89fe34755a7d5d9bb92829dd2a621bca240e9f6250","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:014d6d034","summary":"The site association's path is /a/????????????/get (one ? per ARTIFACT_ID_LEN = 12 character, app_link_path in get_page.rs) and the Android filter's pathPattern is /a/............/get; neither fits /a/<id>/v/<n>/get. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:clax_server_lib_test: shell::get_page::tests::the_app_links_claim_the_get_page_alone ... ok; //crates/clax-server:integration__3: get_page::well_known_served_only_when_configured ... ok; //apps/clax_app:apk_check_test PASSED, //apps/clax_app:apk_test PASSED (apk-check.sh checks the new pathPattern).","supersedes":"b0e3bc2168e0d0a4b03fba6591b3026a777968babb3aa6c09fde56361fe80640","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:42:18.851426Z","id":"7e5518204b62ed2dd9386ec086ff992f99950b68d96d31bbd15613454c865642","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3573f2cfc","summary":"refusals passes on a 403 whose error code is not_for_agents. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__3: get_page::get_page_refuses_the_owners_agent_as_the_contract_says ... ok (daemon token plus X-Clax-Session on spawn_hosted_with answers 403 not_for_agents at /a/<id>/get, /a/<id>/get/ and an unknown ID; the token alone still gets the page; a local daemon answers 403 too); //crates/clax-server:clax_server_lib_test the_contract_route_table_is_the_declared_one ... ok.","supersedes":"c8e50f8cafbce8e10175e99cf38e70995423bfc731dce4b72491134528153e25","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:47:07.109540Z","id":"2f31f029aecb3cd26279dabfcc426716eba347ed0eced3651b51855878922e4d","body":{"detail":"Nothing on the server maps an icon word to a glyph (the web shell does not draw artifact icons either), so the no-script page shows the initial. When an icon set exists, the tile should draw it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"2d94931bcbae16b6f6530d4e5ab31d22ddc926e2802fc71b4047a60a5efa7798"},"summary":"The Get in Clax page draws the title's first letter in its tile; the artifact's icon word is only the tile's title attribute","supersedes":"0d8a4931da73d6c7afddbb9812126303c0544e73bfaed2f3bff1a3e83bcba595","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:47:07.762548Z","id":"a15e6211dc3c87f4da2b62fd19f0372ff21c064287aa5c7eaf328cf1a7f24b56","body":{"detail":"For GET /a/<id>/get, clax_http::hosted::gate answers a restricted page, a page that does not exist and a malformed ID with JSON (404 not_found, 401 sign_in_required) before the handler runs. refusals, layered outside the gate in crates/clax-server/src/router.rs wrap, turns any 401/403/404 of that path that is not text/html into the one 404 page with the /signin link, so the answers stay alike; it reads a 403's body (up to 64 KiB) and passes a not_for_agents refusal on unchanged. The gate itself could render page paths' refusals as pages, for /a/<id> too, which today answers a signed-out browser with JSON.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":336},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"c4dbbb66790143e557f782a7268d1a2ca8b56e939eb8c1f5047edc609740886b"},"summary":"The Get in Clax page's sign-in answer is made by a layer that rewrites the hosted gate's JSON refusals, not by the gate","supersedes":"a6eb1567a5f37fa6ee60488184c14089007f0931fd0af5f1d019e9794a54fb62","tags":["revisit:the hosted gate renders HTML refusals for page paths","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:47:08.526790Z","id":"8fc28d6caba2623b192a9fa5aee8a8271af12e27fdd9f7552d9c3304545b235b","body":{"detail":"refusals recognises an agent's refusal by reading the 403 body's error.code. A HEAD response reaches the layer with its body already empty, so the JSON does not parse and the 403 becomes the unavailable() 404 page. Seen on TestServer::spawn_hosted_with with Authorization: Bearer <daemon token> and X-Clax-Session: s1: GET answered 403 application/json not_for_agents, HEAD answered 404 text/html, for an existing, a never-made and a malformed ID alike (no existence leak). docs/contract.md lists 403 not_for_agents for the route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"f63f73237be3b5010f356bcbd822ab394bfa16cae5504825fd4485719d42c0c5"},"suggested_fix":"Decide on the request rather than the body: answer agents (DeniedToGrants::refuse_agents) before the layer rewrites, e.g. mark the response with an extension in page() that refusals passes through, instead of parsing the body.","summary":"On a hosted Clax the owner's agent gets 403 not_for_agents for GET /a/<id>/get but 404 HTML for HEAD","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.098878Z","id":"803d69fed6cd79d1d7c253c256926b7f99ad8d6107d833288b00765b2ef5eefb","body":{"detail":"byline here prints a.bundle_version, the lineage's release counter (spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.8 'Two counters'), and names the newest bundle's publisher whenever they are not the owner. The artifact page's header (web/shell/src/view/publisher.ts:25-29 appByline, called with a.current_version from lineText) prints the artifact version and names the editor only when their bundle is on the head. Failure: an app whose newest bundle (release 5, by @junp) is on artifact v12, the head, reads \"v12 by @junp · by @akesling\" under its title and \"v5 by @junp · by @akesling\" one tap later on /a/<id>/get; after the owner publishes v13 from the web without a bundle, the header reads \"v13 · by @akesling\" and the get page still \"v5 by @junp · by @akesling\". Spec D7's example (\"v8 by @junp\") is what recipients see in the app, which numbers releases by the bundle counter.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"7e36d93bf75f25faf08c48ce713f0f278a5d47074db6a6694368675ff16790b5"},"suggested_fix":"Pick one counter for the byline on both surfaces (the bundle's release counter matches what the app shows on its update sheet) and one rule for naming the editor; the artifact JSON's app already carries bundle_version and version, so appByline can take the same inputs as byline here.","summary":"The Get in Clax page and the app's header number the same app differently and name its editor by different rules","tags":["app-push","copy","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099741Z","id":"049f7d1114540a55a0907e51410ea9e10f029a4b3b16c6407c1c504bdb2e166c","body":{"detail":"STYLE defines stone colours (--bg #fafaf9, --fg #1c1917, dark --bg #1c1917) that differ from the shell's tokens (web/shell/src/theme.css:19-23 and 57-59: --bg #f7f7f5, --fg #1c1b19, dark --bg #141413), so the step from an app's page to its get page shifts the background and ink. It follows prefers-color-scheme only; a viewer who set Light or Dark with the shell's theme switch (:root[data-theme]) gets the system's theme here. The page runs no script by design, so the choice can reach it only from the server.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"6be0cee872663f6bd5ed09ec418744682bb16c470b9bedc9e99bd44051e92c6c"},"suggested_fix":"Copy the shell's light and dark token values into STYLE; if the theme choice is ever stored in a cookie, set data-theme on <html> from it server-side.","summary":"The Get in Clax page has its own palette and ignores the theme chosen in the shell","tags":["app-push","ui","theme","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/get_page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.101541Z","id":"9c392e172f429228d5b12791a7df5b76ab0ce5e3d3253e5700ad424a0cd47c71","body":{"detail":"The doc comment on apple_app_site_association and crates/clax-worker/README.md:156 say the file lets /a/<id>/get open the iOS and macOS app. apps/clax_app/macos/Runner has no associated-domains entitlement (the ad hoc signed app cannot carry one) and AppDelegate.swift implements no application(_:continue:restorationHandler:), so on a Mac the link opens in the browser and only clax: links reach the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":427},"end":{"line":431},"content_hash":"016788d0e233a3a14ac832aa87fc74908d49e97edc514ea0b0ce6bb4ff1ada13"},"suggested_fix":"Say iOS only, and that the Mac app takes clax: links, until the Mac app is signed with a profile carrying applinks:clax.dev and handles the user activity.","summary":"The site association says it opens the app on macOS, but the Mac app takes no universal links","tags":["docs","links","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:35:28.519814Z","id":"c09195327c45013674a17392860d46a46223b2569e9f09fefd987b9e079183f6","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a hosted daemon (any [hosted] public_origin, the Worker), opening /a/<id> shows an empty or 404 frame for every artifact. The bootstrap emits no frame on a hosted daemon (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs:332-335: the frame needs a site session), and the shell frames frameSite(id, origin) (web/shell/src/origin.ts), which off localhost and 127.0.0.1 has no site origin, so it loads /c/<id>/v/<n>/, which a hosted daemon answers 404 (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs mounts no content routes there; crates/clax-server/tests/api_hosted.rs content_is_served_on_its_site_alone_and_keyed_addresses_are_gone). The server side is in place: POST /api/artifacts/<id>/site-code answers the frame's src, and a frame navigated to the site without a session is signed in through /site-signin with a partitioned cookie (crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_access.rs). Resolved when the shell frames the site origin from the configured site domain through a site code (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5), which must land before any deploy.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"304ff2d346c19dc0e99553b765455e90a7dd0b15d786664b19b411545c72c894"},"summary":"A hosted Clax's artifact page shows no content: the page frames nothing and the shell's frame falls back to a /c/ address the hosted public host no longer serves","tags":["site-origins","hosted","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:44:15.654336Z","id":"68d8fb48d49c4e49fd560250eb5a01cef6a8cf8954e44601f7a22f1d38472ec5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c09195327c45013674a17392860d46a46223b2569e9f09fefd987b9e079183f6","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"304ff2d346c19dc0e99553b765455e90a7dd0b15d786664b19b411545c72c894"},"summary":"The local shell's frames fail too in Chromium: just web-e2e at a300e410 fails //web:e2e_gesture (78) and //web:e2e_rest (328 failed, 62 passed); each waits 10 s in web/e2e/fixtures.ts contentFrame for a frame at <id>.localhost:<port>/_clax/v/<n>/ that never arrives. The frame's navigation goes through /site-signin (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs navigation, framed) and the redirect chain does not end on the page there (not yet diagnosed: the owner cookie on the framed /site-signin request, or the partitioned Secure cookie on http *.localhost, are the candidates). crates/clax-server/tests/api_site_access.rs a_local_shells_frame_signs_itself_in_through_site_signin_partitioned passes the same chain over HTTP. The shell asking POST /api/artifacts/<id>/site-code for its frame's src (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-22-clax-run-site-origins.md Task 5) replaces the chain.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
